{
  "code": "LCP",
  "title": "FCU LCP Checklist",
  "rev": "A",
  "discipline": "ACMV",
  "category": "ITR",
  "scope": "equipment",
  "page": { "size": "A4", "orientation": "portrait" },
  "source": "spec/FCU_LCP_Checklist.html (Rev 0)",

  "variables": [
    { "id": "damper_qty", "label": "Motorized dampers", "type": "number", "default": 2 }
  ],

  "header": {
    "title": "Checklist Details",
    "fields": [
      { "id": "project",  "label": "Project",        "type": "text", "source": "project.name", "readonly": true },
      { "id": "location", "label": "Location",       "type": "text", "source": "equipment.location", "required": true },
      { "id": "ref_code", "label": "Reference Code", "type": "text", "source": "equipment.tag", "required": true },
      { "id": "date",     "label": "Date",           "type": "date", "required": true }
    ]
  },

  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "checks",
      "title": "FCU LCP Checklist",
      "type": "standard",
      "page_break_before": true,
      "columns": {
        "result":  { "label": "Yes / No / NA" },
        "remarks": { "label": "Comments" }
      },
      "allow_add_rows": true,
      "add_row_template": {
        "type": "status",
        "states": [
          { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
          { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
          { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
        ],
        "remarks": true,
        "editable_no": true
      },
      "_note": "The source sheet prints eight worded items followed by three blank numbered rows (9, 10, 11) for whatever else the panel needs. Those blanks are `allow_add_rows`, not three empty template rows: an engineer's added wording is record data, never template wording (SPEC §12, Hard Rule #5), and a record that needs none prints none rather than three empty lines.\n\n`status` rather than `pass_fail_na` so the three columns read Yes / No / NA exactly as the sheet heads them, and so an added row can carry the same words — `add_row_template` has no `labels` key. The outcomes make a \"No\" answer derivable as an outstanding item (SPEC §6).",
      "rows": [
        { "id": "lcp_01", "no": "1", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Incoming power supply available.",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] },
        { "id": "lcp_02", "no": "2", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Switch mode (MAN / OFF / BMS)",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] },
        { "id": "lcp_03", "no": "3", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "RUN / STOP / TRIP Status (BMS)",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] },
        { "id": "lcp_04", "no": "4", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Test Time Schedule (BMS Schedule)",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] },
        { "id": "lcp_05", "no": "5", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Check {{damper_qty}} nos Motorized Damper Status (Open / Close)",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ],
          "_note": "The source hardcodes \"2 nos\"; the damper count varies per FCU, so it is a `{{variable}}` set once per record (SPEC §5.1) rather than wording baked into the template." },
        { "id": "lcp_06", "no": "6", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Chilled water control valve — TA Smart Valve (valve open / close)",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] },
        { "id": "lcp_07", "no": "7", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Control Panel Lamp Test",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] },
        { "id": "lcp_08", "no": "8", "type": "status", "remarks": true,
          "description": "Check LCP status output signals to BMS — termination complete",
          "states": [
            { "value": "yes", "label": "Yes", "outcome": "pass" },
            { "value": "no",  "label": "No",  "outcome": "fail" },
            { "value": "na",  "label": "NA",  "outcome": "na" }
          ] }
      ]
    },

    {
      "id": "measurements",
      "title": "Motor Measurements",
      "type": "field_group",
      "page_break_before": true,
      "_note": "The sheet's single inline strip (V / LOW / MED / HIGH) under the checklist. A field group, not a table: it records one set of readings for this panel, not a list.\n\nThe break here is what gives the checklist room to grow. Everything on one page measured 382.1mm against 297mm — the app's three signature columns are 85.5mm where the source's signature table is a compact strip. Breaking before the measurements leaves the checklist a page of its own with roughly 87mm spare, about six added rows, and still closes the record on page 2 with the signatures rather than spending a third page on them.",
      "fields": [
        { "id": "voltage",      "label": "Voltage",        "type": "number", "unit": "V" },
        { "id": "current_low",  "label": "Current — LOW",  "type": "number", "unit": "A" },
        { "id": "current_med",  "label": "Current — MED",  "type": "number", "unit": "A" },
        { "id": "current_high", "label": "Current — HIGH", "type": "number", "unit": "A" }
      ]
    },

    {
      "id": "remarks",
      "title": "Remarks",
      "type": "field_group",
      "_note": "A field group, not a one-row standard section: a standard section prints its column headers, so a lone remarks row came out headed \"Description | Remarks | Remarks\". The source is a plain labelled box.",
      "fields": [
        { "id": "general_remarks", "label": "Remarks", "type": "textarea" }
      ]
    },

    {
      "id": "sign_off",
      "type": "sign_off",
      "_note": "An in-flow `sign_off` section, not the top-level `footer`: the source is a single A4 portrait sheet that closes with its three signature rows, and portrait leaves enough body height to keep them there. Measured with a full record — see the parity test.",
      "signatures": [
        { "id": "sig_tested",   "role": "Tested By",    "company_default": "Kenyon Pte Ltd", "company_locked": true, "required": true, "stage": "contractor" },
        { "id": "sig_witness",  "role": "Witnessed By", "company_default": "T&C Consultant", "required": false, "stage": "witness" },
        { "id": "sig_client",   "role": "Witnessed By", "company_default": "Client", "required": false, "stage": "client" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
